# Where each store fixture came from, in terms a machine can check.
#
# `engine/tests/upgrade.rs` migrates each of these to the current schema and
# drives its instance, and the value of doing that rests entirely on the
# fixture being what the release's OWN engine wrote. Unlike the tenant vectors
# (tenants/_upgrade/PROVENANCE), a store fixture CANNOT be regenerated: the
# engine that wrote it no longer exists in the tree, and rewriting one with
# today's engine would produce a fixture that tests nothing but today.
#
# So the checkable record is different in kind, and this file says so rather
# than implying the two are equally provable. What is checked, by
# `tools/lint-provenance.sh` as a gate phase:
#
#   * every file is byte for byte what it was at the commit named here, and
#   * that commit is still the LAST commit to touch the directory.
#
# Together those mean the fixture has not been edited since it was recorded --
# edit it in the working tree and the bytes differ; edit it and commit, and the
# last-touching commit moves. Either way the gate fails until the record is
# deliberately updated, which is the same shape as regenerating a golden.
#
# What this does NOT prove is that the fixture was written by the release it
# names. Nothing in the tree can prove that, because the evidence would be the
# engine that is gone; `written_by` is an assertion by the person who made it,
# and it is marked as one here instead of being dressed as a check.
#
# Format: as tenants/_upgrade/PROVENANCE.
#
#   kind        `committed` -- the files are <directory>/<path> at <commit>,
#               and <commit> is the last commit to touch <directory>.
#   commit      the commit that added the fixture, in full.
#   made        the day of that commit, UTC.
#   written_by  the release whose engine wrote the store. AN ASSERTION, not a
#               check; see above.
#   schema      the store schema version the fixture carries. Checked against
#               the directory's own `schema` file, so the two cannot drift.

